# Secrets — never commit. Keys live in the shell env and in GitHub Actions Secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local scratch
scratch/
*.local.json

# NOTE: HALT is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the kill switch, and GitHub
# Actions runs are stateless — the file only survives between ticks by being
# committed. Same reason data/journal.jsonl is committed.

# The SQLite read model IS ignored, for the opposite reason. It holds no fact
# that data/journal.jsonl does not — `python store.py --rebuild` reproduces it
# exactly — so committing it would put a binary blob in the path five people
# rebase through while the Actions cron pushes the journal several times a day.
# JSONL merges; a .db file does not. If this file is ever committed, the
# journal has stopped being the single source of truth.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

.gstack/

# memsearch plugin index and session notes -- local only, never published
.memsearch/

# LaTeX build artifacts (deck/). theta-gate.pdf itself IS committed -- it is
# a submission deliverable, and teammates and judges need it without a TeX
# install. Same for cover/cover.png. Everything below regenerates via `make`.
deck/*.aux
deck/*.log
deck/*.nav
deck/*.out
deck/*.snm
deck/*.toc
deck/*.vrb
deck/build/

# Agent session state. Written by whatever assistant a teammate happens to
# run, at whatever depth -- .omc/ has already appeared at the repo root AND
# inside deck/ during this build. No leading slash, so it matches anywhere.
.omc/

# Claude Code's per-machine permission overrides. The shared
# .claude/settings.json IS committed on purpose -- it is the read-only
# Alpaca allowlist the team relies on, and the file that explicitly denies
# `position close-all`. Only the .local. sibling is personal.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Rehearsal journals and HALT copies from `loop.py --as-of` (see its
# --help). Deliberately NOT data/journal.jsonl or data/HALT.json: a
# rehearsal writes events stamped with a fabricated clock, the real
# journal is the append-only audit trail judges read, and the real
# HALT.json is the live kill switch. Disposable by design.
data/rehearsal-*
